<item><title>Niamey requires permits for new religious-site construction</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niamey-requires-permits-for-new-religious-site-construction-71df7f/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niamey-requires-permits-for-new-religious-site-construction-71df7f/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>An order signed on 17 November also gives existing sites six months to have their situation examined by city services.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:56:30 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niamey-requires-permits-for-new-religious-site-construction-71df7f/share.jpg" length="41032" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niamey-requires-permits-for-new-religious-site-construction-71df7f/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Diffa officials confirm two wholesale markets are complete</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/diffa-officials-confirm-two-wholesale-markets-are-complete-cdcad5/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/diffa-officials-confirm-two-wholesale-markets-are-complete-cdcad5/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>The markets in Goudoumaria and Mainé-Soroa have received provisional acceptance, while supervisors also inspected two roads toward Nigeria.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 23:46:14 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" length="31036" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Zinder governor allocates 15 tonnes of potato seed to 12 communes</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/zinder-governor-allocates-15-tonnes-of-potato-seed-to-12-fc92ef/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/zinder-governor-allocates-15-tonnes-of-potato-seed-to-12-fc92ef/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>The early-maturing variety takes 80 to 90 days to mature, and the regional agriculture director says it yields 30 tonnes per hectare.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:51:25 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" length="31036" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Tiani directs Niger, Mali and Burkina Faso ministers to advance investment work</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/tiani-directs-niger-mali-and-burkina-faso-ministers-to-6c254c/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/tiani-directs-niger-mali-and-burkina-faso-ministers-to-6c254c/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>The three countries’ trade and industry ministers briefed Niger’s president on the Invest in Niger forum, which opened 48 hours earlier.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:05:32 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" length="31036" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
